                <pb facs="0299" n="1033" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1033"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Jóse</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-04-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>After the British occupied Corinto, 27th, town deserted by natives. The
                    Nicaraguan Government stopped railway communication with that port. Pacific Mail
                    steamers have been ordered not to touch there, thus completely isolating town.
                    British seized Government building and archives. Hoisted British flag at that
                    place.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baker.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
